cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Exact Hypergraph Duality for Multi-Rate Lattice Sampling under Common-Mode Drift"
abstract: >-
  A periodic system with period T is sampled by grids, the divisors of T above
  one, and each grid seats the divisors of T in blocks of section classes. This
  package computes, in exact rational arithmetic, the maximum phase margin any
  design of a given period can attain (a closed-form function of T, not a
  constant), the cheapest design attaining a requested margin (an exact
  hypergraph coverage problem), and the fewest shared sections that hold that
  margin. Margins above the instance ceiling are reported as infeasible at any
  cost, by duality rather than by search failure.
authors:
